        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "2.4 程序调试器gdb"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                96,
                43,
                286,
                87
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "2.4.1 gdb简介"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                95,
                131,
                235,
                172
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "gdb是GNU Project Debugger的简称，也是GNU(GNU's Not Unix)开源项目中遵循GPL发行许可证的free software。掌握gdb调试技巧，在项目上遇到问题才会得心应手。gdb 官方网站(https://sourceware.org/gdb/)"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                94,
                188,
                892,
                268
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "一般来说，GDB主要能够提供以下四个方面的帮助："
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                94,
                280,
                441,
                317
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "GDB can do four main kinds of things (plus other things in support of these) to help you catch bugs in the act:"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                94,
                332,
                833,
                368
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": " Start your program, specifying anything that might affect its behavior.(指定—些参数)"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                96,
                384,
                697,
                420
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• Make your program stop on specified conditions. (断点)"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                98,
                435,
                497,
                476
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• Examine what has happened, when your program has stopped.(分析crash现场)"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                96,
                487,
                659,
                520
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• Change things in your program, so you can experiment with correcting the effects of one bug and go on to learn about another.(直接修改程序，看结果)"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                96,
                536,
                869,
                615
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "GDB: The GNU Project Debugger [bugs] [maintainers] [contributing] [current git] [documentation] [download] [home] [irc] [links] [mailing lists] [news] [schedule] [song] [wiki] GDB: The GNU Project Debugger"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                263,
                701,
                639,
                801
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "What is GDB?"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                98,
                811,
                157,
                829
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "GDB, the GNU Project debugger, allows you to see what is going on inside' another program while it executes -- or what another program was doing at the moment it crashed."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                98,
                840,
                664,
                860
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "GDB can do four main kinds of things (plus other things in support of these) to help you catch bugs in the act:"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                98,
                868,
                455,
                889
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• Start your program, specifying anything that might affect its behavior."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                107,
                896,
                344,
                914
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• Make your program stop on specified conditions."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                107,
                912,
                279,
                930
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• Examine what has happened, when your program has stopped."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                107,
                930,
                321,
                945
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• Change things in your program, so you can experiment with correcting the effects of one bug and go on to learn about another."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                107,
                943,
                529,
                963
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Those programs might be executing on the same machine as GDB (native), on another machine (remote), or on a simulator. GDB can run on most popular UNIX and Microsoft Windows variants, as well as on macOS"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                98,
                969,
                785,
                989
            ]
        }
    ]
]